choice ACTRUST_CRYPTO_KEY_PROFILE
    prompt "Persistent private-key profile"
    default ACTRUST_CRYPTO_KEY_PROFILE_DEVELOPMENT
    help
        Select whether persistent private keys may use the software backend or
        must remain non-exportable in a platform TEE / secure element.

config ACTRUST_CRYPTO_KEY_PROFILE_DEVELOPMENT
    bool "Development software keys"
    help
        Permit software-generated private keys serialized through the adapter
        secure store. This profile is for development and reference platforms;
        it does not provide non-exportable private-key storage.

config ACTRUST_CRYPTO_KEY_PROFILE_PRODUCTION
    bool "Strict production hardware keys"
    depends on ACTRUST_SEC_HW_KEY_MGMT && ACTRUST_SEC_HW_ECDSA && ACTRUST_SEC_HW_AES
    help
        Require persistent private keys to use the hardware backend. Crypto
        initialization rejects adapters whose runtime capabilities do not match
        the configured hardware requirements. No hardware-to-software fallback
        is performed.

endchoice
